#{[{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046644} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186520604} :activity/id #uuid "5326f489-c4a2-5092-8c77-6ec4ee9bd4a1" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050797 :topic/id #uuid "67a4c8b0-845c-55dc-ad90-cd6044fd5591" :topic/math-academy-id 969} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186520560 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186520475 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d9f22e8-2426-54ec-8e4d-ceebb5065f00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-1-\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520034} {:answer/id #uuid "46b674e3-477c-5d6b-8938-c0aa7e7328b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1})+1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520097} {:answer/id #uuid "5683b63e-518f-5920-9350-c68914ed0bc4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1})-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520128} {:answer/id #uuid "6c6a5d1c-174d-5af0-a15b-bcbed198a09b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520152} {:answer/id #uuid "f79ae12a-4fbf-5066-b81a-c94e70a59044" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x-1+\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520353}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186520128} :answer-field/id #uuid "2a874508-e5a5-5caf-a21a-b4d69dce3efa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520376}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "7e900458-4a34-53b2-8b6d-fd38c3b57268" :question/math-academy-id "q-125986" :question/problem "Using the definition of the hyperbolic cosine, calculate ${f}^{-1}(x)$ given that $f(x)=\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(x+1)$ and $x\\ge -1.$" :question/worked-solution "Let $y=\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(x+1).$ Since $x\\ge -1,$ we have $y\\ge 1.$\n\nTo find the inverse function we swap $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(y+1),\n$$\n\nwhere $x\\ge 1$ and $y\\ge -1.$\n\nNext, we apply the definition of $\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{y+1}+{e}^{-(y+1)}) \\\\ 2x & ={e}^{y+1}+{e}^{-(y+1)} \\\\ 2x{e}^{y+1} & ={e}^{2(y+1)}+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBringing everything to the left-hand side, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2(y+1)}-2x{e}^{y+1}+1 & =0 \\\\ {({e}^{y+1})}^{2}-2x({e}^{y+1})+1 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $Y={e}^{y+1}.$ We can form a quadratic equation in $Y$ and solve it by completing the square, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Y}^{2}-2xY+1 & =0 \\\\ (Y-x)^{2}-{x}^{2}+1 & =0 \\\\ (Y-x)^{2} & ={x}^{2}-1 \\\\ Y-x & =\\pm \\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1} \\\\ Y & =x\\pm \\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1} \\\\ {e}^{y+1} & =x\\pm \\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1} \\\\ y+1 & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x\\pm \\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that for  $x\\ge 1,$ we have $x-\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}\\le 1$ and  $x+\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}\\ge 1.$ Since $y+1\\ge 0,$ the logarithm in the above equality must be non-negative. This requires its argument to be greater than or equal to $1$ for $x\\ge 1$, so we reject the alternative with the negative sign. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y+1 & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}) \\\\ y & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1})-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1})-1.\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "5ead7583-af5a-50aa-b7c8-b27d60003f5d" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186520574}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186520573 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186520485 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2cca56e0-bd46-5cdc-92e5-fbf4d373740e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t+\\frac{1}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520059} {:answer/id #uuid "4ac055dd-9f86-515e-b1ae-23330cb8d42f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2t+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520104} {:answer/id #uuid "5f33329f-ed6e-55fc-8a52-3418bf264493" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t+\\frac{1}{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520139} {:answer/id #uuid "728d87fa-4ae9-5abf-a254-4e2127b85d13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2t+2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520156} {:answer/id #uuid "72957adc-bbda-5a70-8bcf-de083ff0510a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2t+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520157}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186520157} :answer-field/id #uuid "08605099-e0ee-5781-8ffd-d1bea3536f65" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520370}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "9750db93-431a-52f4-a35e-36e894133bed" :question/math-academy-id "q-125859" :question/problem "$$\n\nGiven that $t>-\\frac{1}{2},$ which of the following is equivalent to $\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(\\frac{t}{t+1})?$" :question/worked-solution "The definition of $\\operatorname{artanh}⁡x$ is \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{artanh}⁡x=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1+x}{1-x}).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(\\frac{t}{t+1}) & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1+\\frac{t}{t+1}}{1-\\frac{t}{t+1}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{\\frac{t+1+t}{t+1}}{\\frac{t+1-t}{t+1}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{\\frac{2t+1}{t+1}}{\\frac{1}{t+1}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2t+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "75b8f4f6-638e-52c0-9e51-b84790620338" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186520560}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186520574 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186520502 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4fbe8f32-b269-5817-8957-1ff911e57228" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\ln(3+2\\sqrt{2})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520113}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186520113} :answer-field/id #uuid "f7cb44d4-8640-5f83-ba9b-96604fc838db" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520442}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "da7e5a10-376b-5a22-a310-bd1bf7fa24cf" :question/math-academy-id "q-300604" :question/problem "$$\n\nEvaluate $\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡3.$ **Do not round** your answer.\n\n$\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡3=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "By definition,\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡x=ln\\,(x+\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡3 & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3+\\sqrt{{3}^{2}-1}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3+\\sqrt{9-1}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3+\\sqrt{8}).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "796ec98d-fdc6-5152-8f17-0c07206d2a8e"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186520596 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186520483 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2645204e-4a2f-5bad-beb3-763d90807c2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520046} {:answer/id #uuid "294f333b-a9d4-562a-8eae-492cfcc89909" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520049} {:answer/id #uuid "536f3405-9be4-55d8-a59a-c53890d35b59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520118} {:answer/id #uuid "66bb441d-dd19-59af-b152-79149e4a3104" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520146} {:answer/id #uuid "c82d5f0d-b3be-5af8-87e6-5da9ad05a797" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520270}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186520049} :answer-field/id #uuid "c6245f27-68e2-534e-b326-9a13a0b95dff" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520423}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "8ddac48b-cef1-5d70-9862-741511be4eb3" :question/math-academy-id "q-125855" :question/problem "$$\n\n$\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(-\\frac{15}{17})=$" :question/worked-solution "The definition of $\\operatorname{artanh}⁡x$ is \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{artanh}⁡x=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1+x}{1-x}).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(-\\frac{15}{17}) & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1+(-\\frac{15}{17})}{1-(-\\frac{15}{17})}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1-\\frac{15}{17}}{1+\\frac{15}{17}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{\\frac{2}{15}}{\\frac{32}{15}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1}{16}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡{2}^{-4} \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "a8b3c09c-22c0-55de-a5ad-4942d464fdf0" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186520573}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186520604 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186520508 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "456e44ed-b28e-597a-8a94-9a42b91da0d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\sqrt{y}+\\sqrt{y-1})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520092} {:answer/id #uuid "4e657d76-cffa-595b-9bca-194435c0c985" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\sqrt{y+1}-\\sqrt{y})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520111} {:answer/id #uuid "786a2bb6-f534-5ec7-b7ad-24c1e39a3327" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\sqrt{y}-\\sqrt{y-1})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520166} {:answer/id #uuid "8086c909-031a-5d75-b37d-adde7d12e254" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\sqrt{y}+\\sqrt{y+1})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520177} {:answer/id #uuid "f593fa3e-303f-519f-8158-523c93d1ab3e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{ln}⁡(y-\\sqrt{y-1})" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520350}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186520092} :answer-field/id #uuid "70bd243f-e07d-55ba-afe6-e9424079d1a3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186520401}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "e77b2e22-83c2-5884-b6a1-4a4bd43f7297" :question/math-academy-id "q-125854" :question/problem "$$\n\nGiven that $y\\ge 1,$ which of the following is equivalent to $\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡\\sqrt{y}?$" :question/worked-solution "The definition of $\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡x$ is \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡\\sqrt{y} & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\sqrt{y}+\\sqrt{{(\\sqrt{y})}^{2}-1}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\sqrt{y}+\\sqrt{y-1}).\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "ca8b15bf-37da-5a6c-b30c-f92d0c220666" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186520596}}] :activity/title "The Inverse Hyperbolic Functions" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186519989}]}
